+## Log Storage Limits
+
+An optional, closed `driver_config.log_limits` object controls newly created
+containers. `max_file_bytes` and `supervisor_tmpfs_bytes` are required integers
+from 1 MiB through 64 MiB; `max_files` is a required integer from 1 through 10.
+The protobuf Struct decoder rejects null, missing fields, unknown fields,
+non-finite numbers, fractional values, and out-of-range values. Omission keeps
+the previous contract rather than silently retargeting retained containers.
+
+The driver selects `json-file`, explicit rotation, no compression, and
+non-blocking delivery through a 256 KiB buffer. It also mounts a root-owned
+mode `0700`, `noexec` tmpfs at `/var/log`. Docker supplies `nodev` and `nosuid`
+for this structured tmpfs mount. User mounts, image volume declarations, the
+workspace, and the configured SSH socket cannot overlap that path. Validation
+rejects template-known errors before image pulls and resource provisioning;
+image-dependent collisions fail before container creation.
+
+The template must have an explicit memory limit and reserve at most half of it
+for this log tmpfs. Installation admission must account for other tmpfs mounts
+and workload memory as well. Rotation thresholds are Docker retention limits,
+not a filesystem quota. Logs can be dropped at buffer saturation, overwritten
+by rotation, or lost when tmpfs stops. Canonical task results need a separate
+durable store. This feature neither changes retained homes nor updates the
+logging configuration of existing containers or the gateway process.
+
+See `docs/reference/sandbox-compute-drivers.mdx` for the public schema.
+
