+### Docker Log Limits
+
+You can bound log storage for new Docker sandboxes by adding `log_limits` to
+the template's `docker` driver-config block. All three fields are required
+integers. OpenShell rejects null, partial objects, unknown fields, and values
+outside these inclusive ranges.
+
+| Field | Range | Purpose |
+|---|---|---|
+| `max_file_bytes` | 1,048,576 through 67,108,864 | Docker JSON log rotation threshold in bytes. |
+| `max_files` | 1 through 10 | Maximum number of retained Docker log files. |
+| `supervisor_tmpfs_bytes` | 1,048,576 through 67,108,864 | Capacity of the supervisor's temporary `/var/log` filesystem. |
+
+This driver-config example selects a 10 MiB rotation threshold, three retained
+files, and 32 MiB of supervisor log storage.
+
+```json
+{
+  "docker": {
+    "log_limits": {
+      "max_file_bytes": 10485760,
+      "max_files": 3,
+      "supervisor_tmpfs_bytes": 33554432
+    }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Set an explicit template memory limit. Supervisor log capacity must not exceed
+half that limit. Budget other tmpfs mounts and workload memory separately.
+OpenShell mounts `/var/log` as root-owned, mode `0700`, non-executable tmpfs.
+User mounts, image `VOLUME` declarations, the OCI working directory, and the
+configured SSH socket must not overlap this path in either direction.
+
+Docker uses the `json-file` logger with compression disabled, non-blocking
+delivery, and a 256 KiB buffer. Rotation discards the oldest Docker logs, and
+a full delivery buffer drops new messages. Supervisor log files share the
+tmpfs capacity and disappear on stop. A full tmpfs prevents further file
+writes; these logs are diagnostic retention, not a durable audit ledger.
+See Docker's [JSON logging](https://docs.docker.com/engine/logging/drivers/json-file/),
+[delivery modes](https://docs.docker.com/engine/logging/configure/#configure-the-delivery-mode-of-log-messages-from-container-to-log-driver),
+and [tmpfs](https://docs.docker.com/engine/storage/tmpfs/) documentation.
+
+Omitting `log_limits` preserves existing Docker defaults. This setting does
+not update or recreate a retained container, change its home or caches, or
+configure the gateway's own logs. Start retains the original container's log
+configuration. Select a new explicitly qualified template when introducing
+these limits, and configure gateway log retention separately.
+
